From e3db2870d47b4d470cd00d9ab5a95175d6223564 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TheCryptoDonkey <TheCryptoDonkey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 07:39:05 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 03/14] feat: link identities to remote NIP-46 signers

Add identity.link-nip46, which links an identity to a bunker:// signer.
The node generates a client keypair, sends connect with the URI's
secret, asks for the user's key, refuses a key the node already holds,
and has the signer sign a throwaway challenge that is fully verified
before the identity file is written. The duplicate check is repeated
under a lock just before the write. The identity keeps a fresh
node-local Ed25519 key for its DID; only the Nostr key is remote.

The new remote_signer module parses bunker URIs (at most 8 relays),
defines the RemoteSigner trait and its typed errors, verifies
remote-signed events against the request, and implements NIP-46 over
nostr-sdk's relay client. Relays get 10 s to accept a connection
(otherwise the signer is reported offline); connect and each request
then get 60 s for the reply, since a person may have to approve on the
device. An auth_url challenge is reported as unsupported.

Identity records gain origin (seed, generated or linked) and the public
half of a linked signer; the client key and the bunker secret never
leave the file. The method is refused from app origins like
identity.nostr-sign, and linked-signer errors pass the RPC error
sanitiser, which now truncates on a character boundary.
